"m01":[{"id":"m01-1","lvl":1,"qs":[{"m":3,"q":"Write 60 as a product of its prime factors."},{"m":2,"q":"Find the highest common factor (HCF) of 18 and 24."},{"m":2,"q":"Find the lowest common multiple (LCM) of 6 and 8."},{"m":3,"q":"Work out 2/3 + 1/4. Give your answer as a fraction."},{"m":3,"q":"Work out 2 1/2 × 3/4. Give your answer as a mixed number."},{"m":3,"q":"(a) Write 0.45 as a fraction in its simplest form.\n(b) Write 7/8 as a decimal."}]},{"id":"m01-2","lvl":2,"qs":[{"m":4,"q":"(a) Write 252 as a product of its prime factors.\n(b) Hence find the smallest positive integer n such that 252n is a square number."},{"m":4,"q":"Find (a) the HCF and (b) the LCM of 84 and 90."},{"m":3,"q":"Bus A leaves the station every 12 minutes. Bus B leaves every 18 minutes. Both leave at 08:00. At what time do they next leave together?"},{"m":3,"q":"Work out 3 1/3 ÷ 1 2/3."},{"m":4,"q":"Write the recurring decimal 0.27 (the digits 27 repeat: 0.272727...) as a fraction in its simplest form."},{"m":3,"q":"Work out 5/6 − 3/8."}]},{"id":"m01-3","lvl":3,"qs":[{"m":5,"q":"The HCF of two numbers is 12 and their LCM is 180. One of the numbers is 36. Find the other number."},{"m":4,"q":"Write the recurring decimal 0.0333... (the 3 repeats) as a fraction in its simplest form."},{"m":4,"q":"Find the smallest positive integer n such that 540n is a cube number."},{"m":4,"q":"Two thirds of a number is 5 more than one half of the same number. Find the number."},{"m":5,"q":"Three lights flash every 4 s, 6 s and 10 s. They all flash together at the start. How many times in the first 5 minutes do they flash together, including the start?"},{"m":4,"q":"Work out (2 1/4 − 1 5/6) ÷ 5/12."}]}],
"m03":[{"id":"m03-1","lvl":1,"qs":[{"m":3,"q":"Round 4.678 (a) to 1 decimal place (b) to 3 significant figures (c) to the nearest whole number."},{"m":2,"q":"The length of a line is 8 cm, correct to the nearest cm. Write down the lower bound and the upper bound."},{"m":2,"q":"x = 3.2 correct to 1 decimal place. Write down the error interval for x."},{"m":3,"q":"A parcel has mass 450 g, to the nearest 10 g. Write down its lower and upper bounds."},{"m":3,"q":"Estimate the value of (49.2 × 3.1) ÷ 0.52 by rounding each number to 1 significant figure."},{"m":3,"q":"n = 60 to the nearest 10. Write down the error interval for n."}]},{"id":"m03-2","lvl":2,"qs":[{"m":3,"q":"a = 6.4 and b = 2.5, both correct to 1 decimal place. Work out the upper bound of a + b."},{"m":3,"q":"a = 6.4 and b = 2.5, both correct to 1 decimal place. Work out the lower bound of a − b."},{"m":4,"q":"A rectangle has length 12.5 cm and width 8.2 cm, both correct to 1 decimal place.\n(a) Work out the upper bound of the area.\n(b) Work out the lower bound of the perimeter."},{"m":4,"q":"A car travels 150 km, to the nearest 10 km, in 2.0 hours, to the nearest 0.1 hour. Work out the upper bound of the average speed. Give your answer to 3 significant figures."},{"m":4,"q":"A metal has mass 240 g (nearest 10 g) and volume 80 cm^3 (nearest 10 cm^3). Work out the lower bound of its density. Give your answer to 3 significant figures."},{"m":4,"q":"a = 12.4 and b = 3.1, both correct to 1 decimal place. Work out the upper and lower bounds of a ÷ b, and decide whether a ÷ b can be given correct to 1 decimal place."}]},{"id":"m03-3","lvl":3,"qs":[{"m":5,"q":"A triangle has sides 7.2 cm and 5.4 cm, each correct to 1 decimal place, and the angle between them is 40° (exact). Work out the lower bound and the upper bound of its area. Give each answer to 3 significant figures."},{"m":4,"q":"The radius of a circle is 6.5 cm, correct to 1 decimal place. Work out the upper bound of the area. Give your answer to 3 significant figures."},{"m":5,"q":"v = u + at, where u = 12.5 (1 d.p.), a = 3.2 (1 d.p.) and t = 5 (nearest whole number). Work out the upper bound of v."},{"m":5,"q":"x = √(a ÷ b), where a = 5.6 and b = 1.4, both correct to 1 decimal place.\nWork out the upper and lower bounds of x to 3 significant figures, and hence write x correct to 1 decimal place, giving a reason."},{"m":4,"q":"A runner covers 100 m (nearest metre) in 12.4 s (nearest 0.1 s). Work out the upper bound of her average speed. Give your answer to 3 significant figures."},{"m":4,"q":"The mass of a coin is 7.5 g, correct to 2 significant figures. 20 identical coins are weighed together. Write down the error interval for the total mass M."}]}],
"m04":[{"id":"m04-1","lvl":1,"qs":[{"m":2,"q":"Find 15% of 240."},{"m":3,"q":"Increase £80 by 20%."},{"m":3,"q":"A coat costs £50. In a sale the price is reduced by 30%. Work out the sale price."},{"m":3,"q":"Write 18 as a percentage of 72."},{"m":3,"q":"Work out the simple interest on £600 invested for 3 years at 4% per year."},{"m":3,"q":"A salary rises from £2400 to £2640. Work out the percentage increase."}]},{"id":"m04-2","lvl":2,"qs":[{"m":3,"q":"After a 15% increase a price is £69. Work out the original price."},{"m":3,"q":"The sale price of a jacket is £42 after a 30% reduction. Work out the original price."},{"m":4,"q":"£2000 is invested at 3% compound interest per year. Work out the value after 4 years."},{"m":4,"q":"A car worth £12 000 loses 15% of its value each year. Work out its value after 3 years."},{"m":3,"q":"Sam buys a bike for £45 and sells it for £63. Work out his percentage profit."},{"m":3,"q":"The price of a meal including 20% VAT is £156. Work out the price before VAT."}]},{"id":"m04-3","lvl":3,"qs":[{"m":5,"q":"A house price increases by 8% in one year and then decreases by 5% in the next. Work out the overall percentage change."},{"m":5,"q":"£5000 is invested at r% compound interest per year. After 2 years it is worth £5512.50. Find r."},{"m":5,"q":"The population of a town is 25 000 and it increases by 4% each year. After how many complete years will it first exceed 30 000?"},{"m":4,"q":"A price is reduced by 20% in a sale. By what percentage must the sale price be increased to return to the original price?"},{"m":4,"q":"A machine loses 12% of its value each year. After 2 years it is worth £15 488. Work out its original value."},{"m":5,"q":"40% of the students in a school are boys. 25% of the boys and 60% of the girls walk to school. What percentage of all the students walk to school?"}]}],
